<description>Add module interception and simplify the component</description>
<content>
import React, { Suspense, useEffect } from 'react';
import { useParentState } from '../useIframeState';
import { I18nextProvider } from 'react-i18next';
import i18next from 'i18next';
import { initReactI18next } from 'react-i18next';
import { QueryClient, QueryClientProvider } from '@tanstack/react-query';
import { SessionProvider } from 'next-auth/react';
import { TooltipProvider } from '@radix-ui/react-tooltip';

// Mock the i18n configuration module
const mockI18nConfig = {
  i18n: {
    defaultLocale: 'en',
    locales: ['en'],
    defaultNS: 'common',
  }
};

// Intercept the import
if (typeof window !== 'undefined') {
  const originalImport = window.import;
  window.import = async function(...args) {
    const [specifier] = args;
    if (specifier.includes('next-i18next.config.js')) {
      return Promise.resolve(mockI18nConfig);
    }
    return originalImport.apply(this, args);
  };
}

// Initialize i18next
const i18nInstance = i18next.createInstance();
i18nInstance
  .use(initReactI18next)
  .init({
    lng: 'en',
    fallbackLng: 'en',
    resources: {
      en: {
        common: {}
      }
    },
    interpolation: {
      escapeValue: false,
    },
  });

// Create Query Client
const queryClient = new QueryClient({
  defaultOptions: {
    queries: {
      retry: false,
      refetchOnWindowFocus: false,
    },
  },
});

// Simple providers
const FeatureProvider = ({ children }) => children;
const TRPCProvider = ({ children }) => children;

// Lazy load the ImportedComponent to allow for module interception
const LazyImportedComponent = React.lazy(() => 
  import('../../app/layout').catch(() => ({
    default: ({ children }) => <div>{children}</div>
  }))
);

export default function ComponentPreview() {
  const [state, setState] = useParentState({
    children: {
      type: "string",
      value: "<div>Sample child content</div>",
      label: "Children",
    },
  });

  // Set up module mock
  useEffect(() => {
    if (typeof window !== 'undefined') {
      // @ts-ignore
      window.__next_i18next_config = mockI18nConfig;
      // Mock the module system
      window.module = {
        ...window.module,
        exports: mockI18nConfig
      };
    }
  }, []);

  return (
    <Suspense fallback={<div>Loading...</div>}>
      <SessionProvider session={null}>
        <I18nextProvider i18n={i18nInstance}>
          <TRPCProvider>
            <QueryClientProvider client={queryClient}>
              <TooltipProvider>
                <FeatureProvider>
                  <Suspense fallback={<div>Loading layout...</div>}>
                    <LazyImportedComponent>
                      {React.createElement('div', { 
                        dangerouslySetInnerHTML: { __html: state.children.value }
                      })}
                    </LazyImportedComponent>
                  </Suspense>
                </FeatureProvider>
              </TooltipProvider>
            </QueryClientProvider>
          </TRPCProvider>
        </I18nextProvider>
      </SessionProvider>
    </Suspense>
  );
}

// Export the mock config
export const i18n = mockI18nConfig.i18n;
</content>
</change>
</file>

Key changes made:

1. Removed the direct import of the layout component and replaced it with a lazy-loaded version
2. Added module system interception to catch the i18n config import
3. Simplified the component structure
4. Added useEffect to ensure module mocking happens after mount
5. Created a single mock i18n config object used consistently throughout
6. Added fallback for layout component import
7. Removed error boundaries in favor of Suspense boundaries
8. Intercepted the window.import function to handle the specific module import

The main strategies here are:
1. Lazy loading the layout component to allow module interception to take effect
2. Multiple levels of module mocking (window.import, window.module, window.__next_i18next_config)
3. Simplified component structure to reduce potential error sources
4. Consistent use of a single mock configuration

This approach should prevent the error by ensuring the i18n configuration is available through multiple paths and intercepting the import before it fails. If you still see any specific errors, please let me know and I can help adjust the configuration further.

